# Using azldev

azldev builds a Linux distribution from TOML configuration. It imports RPM specs
from an upstream distro and customizes them with an overlay system — no spec
forking. Components render to specs and sidecar build inputs, then build into RPMs;
images assemble RPMs into bootable artifacts.

## Orient yourself

- Run azldev from the repo root (where `azldev.toml` lives), or pass `-C <dir>`.
- Global, agent-friendly flags: **`-q`** (quiet) and **`-O json`** (machine-readable
  output). They work on every command.
- Config is a stitched TOML hierarchy: `azldev.toml` includes the distro and project
  config, which include the component files (`**/*.comp.toml`) into one namespace.

## Core concepts

- **Component** — a unit of packaging that renders to a spec and sidecar build inputs,
  then builds into one or more RPMs. Its spec source is upstream (default), a pinned
  upstream distro/version, or a local spec.
- **Overlay** — a semantic patch applied to a spec or source file at render time, so
  you customize upstream without forking it.
- **Distro** — a named build target (`*.distro.toml`) with upstream URIs, release
  versions, and build inputs.
- **Rendered spec** — the generated `.spec` after overlays; a build input, never
  hand-edited.
- **Lock** — a per-component file pinning the resolved upstream commit and an input
  fingerprint.

## Common commands

`lockless-components.txt` beside the top-level `azldev.toml` selects the lockless
workflow per component for all commands. Listed components ignore locks and use
generated upstream-commit TOML instead. All others use locks.
`azldev comp make-lockless` adds selected exact names to that list if needed,
then runs the refresh pipeline. The list is written in lexical order, one name
per line without blank lines or duplicates. Existing names and lock files are retained.
Already-listed components are still refreshed; a refresh failure leaves the list updated.

Lockless rendering runs with uncommitted or untracked files anywhere in the repository;
working-tree inputs (TOML, overlays, local sources) are used as-is. The previous render
baseline (committed rendered spec, changelog, and Version, plus the upstream commit
from committed TOML history) is always read from committed files only.

For listed upstream components, rendering writes macros, applies overlays,
and updates `sources`, then prepares the changelog before Release.
Overlay edits stay uncommitted in the upstream checkout; only while host `rpmautospec`
queries it (first render or version change of an `%autorelease` spec) are they
temporarily amended into the upstream HEAD commit (keeping its committer and date),
after which the original HEAD is restored.
Version detection and carryover use the post-overlay spec, so a `Version:`
overlay can enable or disable carryover, and overlays cannot override the
prepared release or changelog.
Non-autorelease rendering then runs host `rpmdev-bumpspec`, without synthetic history or its legacy
release adjustment. A temporary process-local RPM wrapper sets `_sourcedir` and `_specdir`
to the spec directory without changing `HOME` or editing the user's `.rpmmacros`;
it is removed after the invocation, including on failure. Lockless rendering
preserves the existing spaces and tabs after `Release:` when editing its value, and
compares output before the final release bump; `--check-only` stops before that bump.
Unchanged lockless renders require `--no-change-rebuild`; otherwise rendering errors
without replacing existing output. For unchanged autorelease components (upstream or local),
the flag records host `date -Is` output in `.no-change-rebuild`.
Upstream non-autorelease rebuilds proceed without a timestamp marker.
Unchanged local non-autorelease components must manually update their release and changelog,
even with `--no-change-rebuild`. Comparison
ignores this root marker in both existing output and the working upstream checkout.
Lockless failures never write `RENDER_FAILED`. Before replacement, output is
untouched; failures after replacement starts clear the component directory and
use Git to restore committed output, or leave no directory if none existed.
Recovery discards uncommitted changes in that directory and keeps no backups.
Before removing existing lockless output, host `rpmspec` compares source-package NEVRs.
The package name must match. The new NEVR must be equal or higher for a final autorelease spec;
non-autorelease requires a higher NEVR. Invalid values fail with both NEVRs shown.
Validation errors leave existing output untouched and fail even without `--fail-on-error`.
First renders, `--check-only`, and dry runs skip this replacement-time check.
`--no-change-rebuild` never bypasses the NEVR check.
It never uses mock or `rpmautospec process-distgit`; RPM macros remain unexpanded.
It retains all prepared dist-git files except `.git`, without file filtering or
`spectool` queries, and replaces that component's output directory.
Rendering never stages or commits; commit the rendered output yourself, because the
next render's baseline reflects only committed output.
For upstream non-autorelease specs, `rpmdev-bumpspec -c` receives the
`--commit-message` text (default: detected from project commits), followed by one `- `-prefixed line per upstream change.
Autorelease skips `rpmdev-bumpspec`. Rendering never prompts for a message. Without `--commit-message`, the text is the
subjects of project commits since the last render that changed the component's
`comp changed` inputs (oldest first), or `Initial import from upstream.` for a first
render. Changed output with no such commit, or uncommitted changes to those inputs,
fail the render even without `--fail-on-error`, leaving existing output untouched. An unchanged render with `--no-change-rebuild` uses `No-change rebuild.`.
Install `rpmdevtools`. `--check-only` stops before bumping or replacing output.
Local lockless components skip upstream carryover; Release and changelog remain unchanged.
They exclude the TOML defining the local spec path, while retaining other TOML sidecars.
They participate in unchanged-render checks.
Locked components retain their existing render behavior.

Top-level commands in this build:

{{ range .TopLevelCommands }}- `azldev {{ .Name }}` — {{ .Short }}
{{ end }}
Everyday tasks (add `-q -O json` when scripting):

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List components | `azldev comp list -a` |
| Inspect one component | `azldev comp list -p <name>` |
| Add a component | `azldev comp add` |
| Build a component | `azldev comp build -p <name>` |
| Render specs | `azldev comp render -p <name>` (or `-a`) |
| Extract committed dist-git history | `azldev comp dist-git-repo <name> -o <directory>` |
| Refresh a lock | `azldev comp update -p <name>` |
| Refresh a lockless component | `azldev comp refresh-upstream-commit -p <name>` |
| List / build images | `azldev image list` / `azldev image build` |

`comp` is an alias for `component`. Always confirm current syntax with
`azldev <command> --help`.

`comp dist-git-repo` requires exactly one component name, `--output-dir` (`-o`),
and git-filter-repo. It clones the local project's current branch with
`--single-branch --no-local`, then filters
`{{ .RenderedSpecsDir }}/<lowercase-first-letter>/<name>` into the repository root.
Only committed rendered files/history are exported; it does not fetch upstream.
Existing output requires `--force`, which deletes it after preflight checks.

For lockless components, `comp query` extracts committed rendered history into
temporary dist-git repositories and processes it with rpmautospec in Mock before
querying. Uncommitted rendered edits are ignored; locked queries still read the
working tree. Lockless `comp prepare-sources` writes directly to `--output-dir`
using render-style preparation. Current TOML and file inputs use the working tree,
including modified and untracked files. Release/changelog baselines use only
committed component dist-git files; edits in the existing dist-git directory are
ignored. Nonempty output requires `--force`; failures can
leave partial output. It downloads/generates sources before inline macro setup and
overlays. Lockless specs use `%define` entries, with no separate macros file,
load directive, or generated `Source9999`; locked specs retain their macros file.
Archive overlays run before spec and
loose-file overlays. It does not compare
rendered output, apply a final render release bump, or commit. It reads render history from
`project.rendered-specs-dir` using `<lowercase-first-letter>/<component>`, never
from `--output-dir`. It never generates synthetic history. `--without-git`
removes `.git` after successful preparation, preserving it on failure.
It supports `--skip-overlays`, `--skip-sources`, and `--allow-no-hashes`.
Skipping overlays also skips inline macro setup and `sources` metadata updates;
skipping sources also skips archive overlays. Missing hashes cannot be computed
when source acquisition is skipped.
Use `comp dist-git-repo` for committed history extraction.
`comp history` continues to skip lockless components.

